      "exampleTransliteration": "amsi akaltu l-khubza wa-sharibtu l-ʿaṣīra",
      "exampleEnglish": "Yesterday I ate bread and drank juice.",
      "grammarNote": "شرب's past tense is fully regular too, reading exactly like شَرِبْتُ، شَرِبَ، شَرِبْنَا next to أَكَلْتُ، أَكَلَ، أَكَلْنَا — every verb drilled across levels 21–29 in both tenses (ذهب، أراد، قرأ، أكل، شرب) turns out simpler in the past tense, since one suffix set (ـتُ/ـتَ/ـتِ/ـَ/ـَتْ/ـنَا) covers every regular verb with no vowel-pattern prefix to learn. This sentence reuses وَ from level 20 to join two full past-tense clauses — the same capstone structure, now with a different tense entirely.",
